SGI Octane / IP30 physical-hardware handoff
==========================================

Status: PENDING PHYSICAL HARDWARE
Source revision pin: 1bee7e44579
Branch: topic/sgimips-octane

This handoff stops at the M4a read-only root proof.  Do not boot M4b,
M4c or M4d on the physical machine, do not remount root read-write, and
do not create or truncate files.  Physical power-loss testing is a later
checkpoint.

Serial console
--------------

Use IOC3's first serial port, the one selected by the PROM console
variable.  Force the serial profile and disable autoload:

    setenv -f console d
    setenv AutoLoad No

If the console was previously `g`, power-cycle after changing it so the
PROM starts on serial.

Line settings: 9600 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, no RTS/CTS
and no XON/XOFF.  This is the IOC3 UART A console at kernel address
0x1f620178; the driver reports rate=9600, lcr=0x3, predivider=6 and
divisor=48.  Capture the raw serial stream to a file.  A null-modem cable
is assumed where the host terminal is DTE.

