The root image is 8 GiB; its SGI label has root partition 0 starting at
sector 8256 with 16703488 sectors.  The destination physical drive must
be at least 8 GiB, but its actual capacity is whatever the drive reports:
the guest's `sd0` line and `diskinfo` are expected to show the physical
capacity, not necessarily 8192 MB.  The root partition itself remains the
8 GiB image partition.  Write only to a known disposable SCSI disk at
target 1; this is host-side preparation, not guest write testing.

M3d3 is emulator-only
---------------------

The M3d3 diagnostic is not a physical-hardware artifact.  Its test requires
exactly 32768 x 512-byte sectors and the inquiry identity
`SGI / IRIS EMUL DISK / 1.0`; writing that image to a physical disk changes
neither the disk's identity nor its capacity.  Do not use the M3d3 kernel
or the 16 MiB test image on physical hardware until a separate physical
diagnostic exists.  The retained M3d3 hashes are emulator evidence only:

