Network boot
------------

Serve the selected kernel from a BOOTP/TFTP server.  Rename the pinned
artifact according to the server's BOOTP filename, for example:

    netbsd-XIRI_IP30_M4A_PHYS

At the PROM Command Monitor, use:

    setenv -f console d
    setenv AutoLoad No
    boot -f bootp():netbsd-XIRI_IP30_M4A_PHYS --s

The `--s` is required for M4A: it selects single-user read-only root.  If
the local PROM requires a server address in the bootp specifier, use its
normal `bootp()<server>:<filename>` form; the filename must remain the
same.

