Stage terminal states and return to PROM
----------------------------------------

  M1, M2a
    These kernels deliberately spin in `xiri_ip30_halt()`.  They do not
    return to the PROM and there is no console command that can resume the
    PROM.  Reset from the front panel or power-cycle after recording the
    marker.

  M2b through M3d2
    These checkpoints continue running after their test completes and
    reach the `root device:` prompt (`use one of: halt reboot`).  At that
    prompt type `halt` and wait for the PROM `Option?` menu; do not type
    `reboot`.  If the prompt is not reached, reset.  No disk is required
    for these staged checks.  M3d1/M3d2 exercise the QLogic controllers but
    do not require an attached disk.

  M3d3
    Emulator-only.  Do not run this on physical hardware.  In the emulator
    its disk-test thread ends with `kthread_exit()` while the kernel
    continues to the `root device:` prompt; use `halt` there.  The 16 MiB
    test disk is never a physical root disk.

  M4a
    Single-user read-only shell on the physical root disk.  Record the
    boot and gate checks, then run `shutdown -h now` and wait for
    `unmounting done` and the PROM `Option?` menu.  Do not remount root
    read-write.  If shutdown does not return to the PROM, reset.

Disk attachments by stage
-------------------------

  M1-M3c1   no disk required.
  M3d1-M3d2 no disk required; QLogic controllers only.
  M3d3      emulator-only 16 MiB diagnostic; never physical.
  M4a       prepared 8 GiB-or-larger disposable disk at SCSI target 1;
            root partition sd0a read-only.

M4a read-only gate
------------------

At the shell prompt, record and check:

    uname -a
    /sbin/mount
    ls -l /dev/console
    tty
    stty -a
    vmstat -i
    ls -l /dev/sd0a /dev/sd0b 2>/dev/null

Required observations:

  * `root on sd0a` (the physical config has `dumps on none`, so there is
    no `dumps on` suffix)
  * `Enter pathname of shell or RETURN for /bin/sh:`
  * `root_device on / type ffs (read-only, local)`
  * `/dev/console` is a character device
  * interactive input echoes and commands produce output
  * `com0 rxintr` and `com0 txintr` are present and advancing
  * `sd0` reports the prepared physical drive's identity and capacity;
    the root partition is the 8 GiB image partition

Do not run `mount -u -w /`, `mkdir`, `touch`, `printf > file`, `truncate`,
`mknod`, or any M4b/M4c/M4d command.  A clean `shutdown -h now` is allowed
after recording the read-only result; otherwise reset from the PROM.  A
write-capable or multi-user boot is not part of this handoff.

Evidence to retain
------------------

  * physical machine serial, CPU, RAM, PROM version and `hinv`
  * physical disk model, actual capacity and SCSI target assignment
  * raw serial capture and PROM command transcript
  * SHA-256 of the kernel, root image and TFTP file actually used
  * stage marker, terminal state and elapsed time for each checked stage
  * M4a read-only `mount`, console, TTY and interrupt evidence
  * any failure verbatim; do not substitute an emulator result

Physical hardware and physical power-loss recovery remain separate
checkpoints.  The emulated M4b/M4c/M4d evidence is not a substitute for
physical validation.  The physical M4a config was preflighted in the
emulator at ../xiri/.work/octane-m4a-phys-readonly-20261116; that run
confirms `root on sd0a` and the read-only shell, but is not physical
hardware evidence.
